{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5405-\u200bthought-exercise-rules-as-written-vs-rules-as-intended-subject-mantle","id":5405,"title":"\u200bThought Exercise, Rules as Written vs Rules as Intended. Subject: Mantle","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-07T14:07:36-08:00","id":5405,"title":"\u200bThought Exercise, Rules as Written vs Rules as Intended. Subject: Mantle","content":"Reviewing the full text of the merit today, I'm led to believe there's actually not a limitation in place that technically prohibits a character from purchasing the Merit more than once, and selecting a different court.<br /> <br /> \u200bBy the text of the Merit, a PC doesn't have to be a member of the court, to benefit from Mantle, and there's not a rule that prevents it from being purchased because Mantle (Spring) is not Mantle (Winter). They're *technically* separate merits.<br /> <br /> So a character *could* be Autumn/Winter for example, technically, I believe per RAW (but not RAI).<br /> <br /> To everyone else: Thoughts on this kind of comparison, have I missed something per the RAW?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img835/1264/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Do you see over yonder, friend Sancho, thirty or forty hulking giants? I intend to do battle with them and slay them.&quot;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/441-nighttrace","name":"NightTrace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar441_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T14:43:58-08:00","id":5427,"title":"","content":"Clearly, this was deliberately included so you can have a King Of All who's taken over all the courts and has five dots in everything, and is probably one bad day away from going True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T15:49:48-08:00","id":5500,"title":"","content":"The intent is that you can only buy Mantle if you are part of a Court. Maybe this isn't listed in the Merit, but the last paragraph of page 45 notes that the gaining of a Mantle is the result of the pledge sworn to join the court. Asuming that this pledge is the only way to gain Mantle and that one can only be part of one Court I conclude that a Changeling can only have one Mantle.<br /> <br /> Also, the sidebar on page 94 notes that a Changeling loses her old Court Mantle when switching Courts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T17:45:08-08:00","id":5615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5405-\u200bthought-exercise-rules-as-written-vs-rules-as-intended-subject-mantle?p=5500#post5500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The intent is that you can only buy Mantle if you are part of a Court. Maybe this isn't listed in the Merit, but the last paragraph of page 45 notes that the gaining of a Mantle is the result of the pledge sworn to join the court.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting is that Autumn Nightmares points out the eminent possibility that a changeling could swear an oath to a representative of the season in question other than a local Court.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-07T18:14:47-08:00","id":5635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5405-\u200bthought-exercise-rules-as-written-vs-rules-as-intended-subject-mantle?p=5500#post5500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the sidebar on page 94 notes that a Changeling loses her old Court Mantle when switching Courts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that the sidebar uses &quot;shift&quot; as in &quot;shift allegiance&quot;. But swearing oaths to two courts is <i>not</i> shifting. It's maintaining two allegiances simultaneously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/210-siven","name":"Siven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar210_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T05:48:28-08:00","id":5838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5405-\u200bthought-exercise-rules-as-written-vs-rules-as-intended-subject-mantle?p=5427#post5427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clearly, this was deliberately included so you can have a King Of All who's taken over all the courts and has five dots in everything, and is probably one bad day away from going True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, it's obviously a discussion of a topic of RAW vs RAI. The Rules as Intended? I'm firmly of the opinion that it wasn't supposed to happen. Though, I admit that I think there's some interesting story possibilities from a character with dueling inspirations/leading inspirations. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img835/1264/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Do you see over yonder, friend Sancho, thirty or forty hulking giants? I intend to do battle with them and slay them.&quot;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/441-nighttrace","name":"NightTrace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar441_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T05:07:23-08:00","id":13333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Siven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5405-\u200bthought-exercise-rules-as-written-vs-rules-as-intended-subject-mantle?p=5635#post5635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Note that the sidebar uses &quot;shift&quot; as in &quot;shift allegiance&quot;. But swearing oaths to two courts is <i>not</i> shifting. It's maintaining two allegiances simultaneously.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can only swear complete loyalty to one Season. If its shared then its not complete loyalty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T14:42:18-08:00","id":27541,"title":"","content":"Isn't Court Goodwill representative of multiple Alliances beyond what Mantle provides?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T13:22:40-08:00","id":28246,"title":"","content":"Goodwill is representative of the connections/feelings of the Court in question, however Courts are the sociopolitical groups that formed around people who share a standard ideal/mantle. Mantle in and of itself is a choice of the Wyrd, and doesn't indicate any alliance/allegiance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img835/1264/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">&quot;</span></span><span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Do you see over yonder, friend Sancho, thirty or forty hulking giants? I intend to do battle with them and slay them.&quot;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/441-nighttrace","name":"NightTrace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar441_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T13:46:21-08:00","id":28270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NightTrace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/5405-\u200bthought-exercise-rules-as-written-vs-rules-as-intended-subject-mantle?p=28246#post28246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Goodwill is representative of the connections/feelings of the Court in question, however Courts are the sociopolitical groups that formed around people who share a standard ideal/mantle. Mantle in and of itself is a choice of the Wyrd, and doesn't indicate any alliance/allegiance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mantle constitutes a sworn oath. In conventional freeholds that oath is one of fealty to a monarch. Other sources of Mantle necessitate similar degrees of &quot;payment.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-11T23:43:10-08:00","id":28567,"title":"","content":"At the end of the day, the idea behind mantle seems to necessitate that maintaining the ideals of more than one court should prove nigh-impossible.<br /> <br /> The rules don't seem to imply this as strongly as they should, I'd say.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-12T09:48:32-08:00","id":28783,"title":"","content":"Mantle was intended to be a Wyrd reflection of how much you embody the ideals of your chosen season. Court politics may produce loners and outcasts who might have high Mantle ratings, but very low Court ratings. For example, imagine a courtier of Winter who is so paranoid and silent, they abandon contact with other Changelings and live a monk-like existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1649-null_channel","name":"null_channel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1649_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-25T05:58:45-08:00","id":57375,"title":"","content":"&quot;Characters with no Court cannot purchase Mantle&quot; CtL p97. Also in Grim Fears Auntie Ally is a Winter Court member, who has Mantle (Spring). I think this one is best left to the gaming group to decide. If you have a really good reason to have mantle different than your court the it can make an interesting character. Personally as a GM I'd expect the player to come up with a really good backstory.<br /> <br /> There is no separate mention about taking the merit more than once, but there is this phrase from the same page:<br /> &quot;Should his Mantle fall or he adopt the Mantle of a new Court...&quot;<br /> The text does't mention keeping your mantle and getting a new one at the same time, so I believe that the intention is that you can have only one mantle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2095-daider-santo","name":"Daider Santo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2095_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}